!
! The 0.08889% assurance fee on a sale, in Trebago (fairground_rules.h
! FR1, pay_assure.h F1): floor(amount * 8889 / 10000000), amount in
! integer minor units, one sale per row. Trebago is exact and has no
! floor, and amount * 8889 passes 64 bits near the top of the range, so
! the amount is split: h = floor(amount / 10^7), counted three digits at
! a time (each digit the count of k = 1 to 999 with k * scale <= x, which
! min(1, max(0, x - k * scale + 1)) is for integers), and l the rest,
! below 10^7. Then the fee is h * 8889 + floor(l * 8889 / 10^7), the last
! part 0..8888 counted the same way. ok is 1 for an amount of 0 to
! 2^53 - 1 (ZXV_AMOUNT_MAX) and 0 outside, and the fee is divided by it:
! refused. fee.sutra holds 15 digits: past them the two disagree and the
! fee is held.
trebago assurance_fee
  in  amount(n)
  out fee(n)
  var x(n), a(n), b(n), c(n), s(n), d(n), ok(n)
  ok(i) = min(1, max(0, amount(i) + 1)) * min(1, max(0, 9007199254740991 - amount(i) + 1))
  x(i) = amount(i)
  a(i) = sum(k = 1:999, min(1, max(0, x(i) - k * 10000000000000 + 1)))
  x(i) = x(i) - a(i) * 10000000000000
  b(i) = sum(k = 1:999, min(1, max(0, x(i) - k * 10000000000 + 1)))
  x(i) = x(i) - b(i) * 10000000000
  c(i) = sum(k = 1:999, min(1, max(0, x(i) - k * 10000000 + 1)))
  x(i) = x(i) - c(i) * 10000000
  s(i) = x(i) * 8889
  d(i) = sum(k = 1:8888, min(1, max(0, s(i) - k * 10000000 + 1)))
  fee(i) = ((a(i) * 1000000 + b(i) * 1000 + c(i)) * 8889 + d(i)) / ok(i)
end
